WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.984
Before I could react, Fritz raised his gun to his shoulder and fired at the shark.

2
00:00:04.985 --> 00:00:09.594
The monstrous fish disappeared under the water, and our sheep was safe.

3
00:00:09.595 --> 00:00:11.535
"Well done!" I cried.

4
00:00:11.536 --> 00:00:14.419
Fritz's eyes sparkled at my praise.

5
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:18.848
He carefully watched the water for the shark, but it didn't reappear.

6
00:00:18.849 --> 00:00:26.079
With a breeze in our sail, we quickly reached shore where I released the animals.

7
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.912
My wife and the three younger boys came running to meet us.

8
00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:33.953
They helped to collect the animals and unload supplies from our boat.

9
00:00:33.954 --> 00:00:39.012
We were hungry, but when we reached camp, there was no sign of supper.

10
00:00:39.013 --> 00:00:44.028
"Fritz and I can supply some ham," I volunteered, pointing to the supplies from the ship.

11
00:00:44.029 --> 00:00:48.713
My wife smiled. "Ernest, let's see if we can conjure up some eggs."

12
00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:54.718
"Where did you get these?" I asked as Ernest proudly set before me a dozen turtle eggs.

13
00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:59.799
"I'll tell you over supper when I describe how we spent our day," said my wife.

14
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.817
Supper consisted of an omelet followed by ham and cheese.

15
00:01:03.818 --> 00:01:11.068
After I told the others about our adventures with the animals and shark, my wife began her story.

16
00:01:11.069 --> 00:01:16.427
"The sun beats down on this bare, rocky spot all day," she said.

17
00:01:16.428 --> 00:01:19.081
"And it's even hotter inside the tent.

18
00:01:19.082 --> 00:01:24.499
I decided that you and Fritz weren't the only ones who could do something for this family."

19
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.497
So she and the boys had set out to find a cooler place to live.

20
00:01:28.498 --> 00:01:34.091
Accompanied by the two dogs, they'd crossed the stream and the field of tall grass.

21
00:01:34.092 --> 00:01:37.432
"We soon came to a grove of a dozen trees.

22
00:01:37.433 --> 00:01:42.342
I really can't describe how huge and strange they were," my wife continued.

23
00:01:42.343 --> 00:01:45.332
"Their roots arched above the ground."

24
00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:51.525
She told how Jack had scrambled up above the roots of one tree and measured its circumference with a piece of string.

25
00:01:51.526 --> 00:01:55.915
"I think it was eighteen yards around!" said Jack.

26
00:01:55.916 --> 00:02:02.632
The spot was shady and cool, and the longer they'd stayed there, the more my wife had liked it.

27
00:02:02.633 --> 00:02:11.140
"If only we could live among the branches of those grand, noble trees, I'd feel perfectly safe and happy," she said.

28
00:02:11.141 --> 00:02:15.344
She'd liked the place so much that she didn't feel the need to search anymore.

29
00:02:15.345 --> 00:02:18.267
They'd returned home by way of the beach.

30
00:02:18.268 --> 00:02:21.489
"That's where we found the eggs!" said Ernest.

31
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.664
"Or I should say, the dogs found them."

32
00:02:24.665 --> 00:02:30.673
Everyone laughed. The boys went off to play while my wife and I continued to talk.

33
00:02:30.674 --> 00:02:37.645
"I hope you're in favor of packing everything up and taking us to live among my splendid trees," said Mother.

34
00:02:37.646 --> 00:02:41.552
"So you want us to perch in these trees like birds?" I said.

35
00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:45.187
"If we had wings, it would be a wonderful idea."

36
00:02:45.188 --> 00:02:48.363
"My idea is not as silly as you think.

37
00:02:48.364 --> 00:02:52.046
A house among the branches would keep us safe from wild animals.

38
00:02:52.047 --> 00:02:54.586
And I've seen such a house in Switzerland.

39
00:02:54.587 --> 00:02:57.352
I climbed a staircase to reach it."

40
00:02:57.353 --> 00:03:02.000
I was reluctant to leave our current spot, which was protected by high cliffs.

41
00:03:02.001 --> 00:03:05.852
But my wife continued to make her argument for a house in the treetops.

42
00:03:05.853 --> 00:03:07.512
At last I agreed.

43
00:03:07.513 --> 00:03:13.447
"We'll have to build a bridge first," I said, "in order to carry everything across the stream."

44
00:03:13.448 --> 00:03:15.923
"A bridge!" she exclaimed.

45
00:03:15.924 --> 00:03:19.271
"I'll die from the heat if I have to wait for a bridge."

46
00:03:19.272 --> 00:03:23.295
"We'll need bags and baskets to carry everything," I said.

47
00:03:23.296 --> 00:03:31.203
"If you focus on those, I promise the boys and I will make a bridge as quickly as possible."

48
00:03:31.204 --> 00:03:35.820
So the next day everyone set to work.

49
00:03:35.821 --> 00:03:41.266
Using planks that had washed up from the wreck, we soon completed our bridge.

50
00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:47.048
When moving day arrived, everyone was busy. Some collected provisions.

51
00:03:47.049 --> 00:03:52.507
Others packed kitchen utensils and tools into baskets tied onto the cow and donkey.

52
00:03:52.508 --> 00:03:56.656
We planned to return later for the ducks and geese.

53
00:03:56.657 --> 00:04:00.893
"Leave room for Franz to ride on the donkey!" my wife called out.

54
00:04:00.894 --> 00:04:04.659
"Oh! I almost forgot the chickens and pigeons!"

55
00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:08.089
Away ran the boys to catch the chickens and pigeons.

56
00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:12.746
The result was a lot of chasing, fluttering, cackling, and cooing.

57
00:04:12.747 --> 00:04:14.881
But they didn't catch any of them.

58
00:04:14.882 --> 00:04:19.471
At last my wife scattered some grain inside the tent.

59
00:04:19.472 --> 00:04:26.946
Lured by the food, the chickens and pigeons were easily caught, tied together, and placed on the cow's back.

60
00:04:26.947 --> 00:04:32.028
And off we went! Fritz and my wife led the caravan.

61
00:04:32.029 --> 00:04:35.741
Then came Franz on the donkey, followed by the cow.

62
00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:39.065
Jack led the goats with Knips riding one of them.

63
00:04:39.066 --> 00:04:41.742
Ernest was in charge of the sheep.

64
00:04:41.743 --> 00:04:49.037
I brought up the rear while the two dogs raced back and forth.

65
00:04:49.038 --> 00:04:56.723
Meanwhile the pig stubbornly refused to join us.

66
00:04:56.724 --> 00:05:01.980
We had just crossed the bridge when I heard the pig grunting and squealing angrily behind us.

67
00:05:01.981 --> 00:05:14.917
She had decided to come with us after all, but she clearly wasn't happy about it.

